  "product": {
    "productType": "DAYTOUR",
    "name": "Adelaide Hills Village to Village e-Bike Easy Self-Guided Tour",
    "shortDescription": "Discover the Adelaide Hills on a self-guided e-Bike tour starting in Uraidla. Enjoy an introduction to e-Bikes, ride through Piccadilly Valley, and visit cellar doors and cafes. End your adventure at the historic Uraidla Hotel. ",
    "description": "<p><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Adelaide Hills Village to Village e-Bike Easy Self-Guided Tour</span></b></p><p><b><br></b></p><p><b>Departure Location</b><br></p><p>Uraidla&nbsp;Republic Bakery, 1196 Greenhill Road, Uraidla, South Australia. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>A scenic 17km drive from Adelaide city.&nbsp;</p><p><b><br></b></p><p><b>Duration: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</b>2&nbsp;hours (approx.)</p><p><b>Riding&nbsp;time:</b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 43 minutes at a relaxed pace</p><p><b>Distance:&nbsp;</b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 9.28km</p><p><b>Meeting Time:</b>&nbsp; &nbsp; Flexible hours ask us. &nbsp;Default time 9.00am till 4.00pm&nbsp;<br></p><p><b>Suitable for: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</b>Beginner, naturally fit, casual and seasoned rider</p><p><br></p><p><b>Highlights</b><br></p><ul><li><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">The Piccadilly Valley skirted&nbsp;with vineyards, orchards market gardens and native bush&nbsp;</span></li><li>Skirting Mount Bonython on a quiet gravel road&nbsp;</li><li><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Riding alongside the majestic Cleland National Park&nbsp;</span></li><li>Travel through the&nbsp;quaint country village of Summertown to Uraidla</li></ul><p><br></p><p><b>Highlights on Route</b><br></p><p>Opening hours listed below were correct at the time of printing. &nbsp;Best to view websites to confirm opening hours or to pre book a meal or cellar door wine tasting so as not to be disappointed on the day.</p><p><br></p><p><b>Uraidla Republic Bakery &amp; Brewery</b><br></p><p>Why not arrive extra early and enjoy a cuppa and a bite to eat before your e-Bike adventure begins. &nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.uraidlabakery.com.au/\">https://www.uraidlabakery.com.au/</a><br></p><p>Open 7 days 7.00am till 4.00pm</p><br><p><b>The Piccadilly Valley&nbsp;</b></p><p>Skirted with vineyards, orchards market gardens and pockets of native bush. This area is renowned internationally as one of Australia’s most vibrant cool climate wine regions and&nbsp;stunning scenery.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><b>Cleland National Park</b></p><p>An important con­servation area of bush­land sit­u­at­ed in the Ade­laide Hills face zone with a&nbsp;fan­tas­tic net­work of walk­ing and cycling trails intro­ducing you to the diverse native wildlife, cul­tur­al her­itage and spec­tac­u­lar views of the Ade­laide Hills and&nbsp;surrounds. The flo­ra on the high­er slopes is pre­dom­i­nant­ly stringy­bark for­est with a&nbsp;com­plex under­storey of small trees and shrubs.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.parks.sa.gov.au/parks/cleland-national-park\">parks.sa.gov.au/parks/cleland-national-park</a></p><p>Open 7 days Gates open 9.30am till 5.00pm</p><p><br></p><p><b>Greenhill Wines</b></p><p>Greenhill Wines is a vineyard, cellar door and café situated in the Piccadilly Valley region of the Adelaide Hills 590m above the city. The beautiful landscape is reflected in the wine, food and strong community in the region. Rub shoulders with the locals and be a resident for a&nbsp;few hours.&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://greenhillwines.com.au/\">greenhillwines.com.au</a></p><p>Open&nbsp;Friday to Sunday, 11am till 5pm &nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><b>Hills Collide</b><br></p><p>Hills Collide is a cellar door and wine bar in Summertown run by winemaker Mitchell Fitzpatrick and wine bar owner Shane Ettridge who take a considered and sustainable approach to minimalist winemaking. &nbsp;The kitchen prioritises high-quality, locally sourced produce from the Adelaide Hills and surrounding regions.</p><p>Open see website&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://hillscollide.com/pages/book-now\">https://hillscollide.com/pages/book-now</a></p><p><br></p><p><b>Wotton Family Wines &amp; Summer Cherries &nbsp;</b></p><p>For over 150 years the Wotton family have worked productive, rolling farm land at Uraidla in the Adelaide Hill’s picturesque Piccadilly Valley. &nbsp; In the summer season their cherries are the best. &nbsp;In 1994, the first wine grapes were planted in fertile soils previously used for fruit growing and market gardening. Drop in or book a wine tasting at their cellar door and in summer look out for their 'Open' farm gate sign to purchase mouth watering cherries. &nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.wottonfamilywines.com.au/\">wottonfamilywines.com.au</a></p><p>Open&nbsp;Friday to Sunday, 11am till 5pm</p><p><br></p><p><b>Uraidla Hotel</b></p><p><b>The Uraidla Hotel … the heart of the Community</b><br></p><p>A perfect place to end the day after your e-Bike tour is to drop in next door to the historic and award-winning&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.uraidlahotel.com.au/\"><b>Uraidla Hotel</b></a>, a vibrant heart of the local community, committed to sustainability and eco-friendly practices with great food, local drinks and atmosphere in a welcoming community.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Meals may be pre-booked in the restaurant or just walk in for a great pub meal.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Wine tasting in ‘The Tank’ may be pre-booked with the sommelier to view one of the most extensive wine collections in the Adelaide Hills, featuring a curated selection of local Adelaide Hills wines, national treasures and international icons.</p><p><a href=\"https://uraidlahotel.com.au/\">uraidlahotel.com.au</a><br></p><p>Open 7 days, 11.30am till late</p><p><br></p><p><b>Inclusions</b></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Induction to e-Bike features, fit out and group road riding skills chat&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All day hire of e-Bike and equipment – return anytime up to 4.00pm<br></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A mobile phone holder mounted on e-Bike handlebar</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Digital mobile phone route map for your mobile phone</p><p>· &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; e-Bike, helmet, bike lock, fluorescent vest, pannier bag, cycling gloves</p><p><br></p><p><b>&nbsp;</b></p><p><b>&nbsp;Important Information</b></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Riders must be at least 156cm tall&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Riders to hold a valid drivers licence; photo ID may be required and photographed</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Parent/Guardian participating may enquire if teenage children may also participate&nbsp;</p><p>. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Punctuality essential</p><p><b>&nbsp;</b><br></p><p><b>Cancellation</b></p><p>· &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; A full refund any time up to&nbsp;48 hours prior to Tour start</p><p>. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Tours will be postponed or cancelled on extreme or catastrophic weather days<br></p><p><b>&nbsp;</b><br></p><p><b>Dress Code</b></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Closed in footwear essential<b></b></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Comfortable clothing for outdoor activity, suitable for the weather<b></b></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b>What to bring</b></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Water&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sunscreen</p><p><br></p><p></p>",
